{"text": "The loss of insect life from the food chain. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Would not just be disastrous for wildlife. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It would also have direct consequences. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For the human food supply. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Most Europeans and North Americans are disgusted. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> By the prospect of eating insects. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Which is odd. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Since they consume prawns. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Which are broadly similar. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Being segmented. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And with an external skeleton. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Their ancient ancestors would certainly have eaten insects. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Globally, however. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Eating insects is the norm. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And in some countries. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Insects make up a significant proportion of the diet. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Roughly 80 per cent of the worlds population. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Regularly consume insects. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> With the practice very common. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In South America, Africa and Asia. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And among the native peoples of Oceania. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Approximately 2, 000 different insect species. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Are regularly eaten by people. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Including caterpillars, beetle grubs, ants, wasps. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Moth pupae, stink bugs, grasshoppers and crickets. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To give an example. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It is estimated. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That 1, 600 tons of mopane worms are sold. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For human consumption. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In South Africa each year. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> With many more privately collected and consumed.", "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "e", " ", "l", "o", "s", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "i", "n", "s", "e", "c", "t", " ", "l", "i", "f", "e", " ", "f", "r", "o", "m", " ", "t", "h", "e", 